From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shikosu <teovidal01@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 20:31:47 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Linux host: Horizon records the calls that make memory
 executable, the report says where the JIT was entered, and the tests for
 generated code across threads (#17)

horizon_hle: SetMemoryPermission (with the X bit), SetProcessMemoryPermission, ControlCodeMemory, CreateCodeMemory,
MapProcessCodeMemory and UnmapProcessCodeMemory are named, counted and recorded (the first 200, addresses and numbers
only), the first of each kind is logged as [dyncode], and code_summary() feeds the run report. The code-memory calls
were unhandled before and still answer R_NOT_IMPLEMENTED. aot_report.jit_targets() splits the JIT entries
(Aot.jit_log) into those inside a module image and those outside every module, which is what generated code looks
like. horizon_run.py prints the counts at the end of a run and puts both in --report-json.

test_aot_dynamic_code.py: a thread that ran generated code sees a rewrite made by another thread (a store of guest
code, or the harness), and the dc cvau / ic ivau / isb sequence runs. With the cross-thread invalidation of
aot_jit.cpp turned off on purpose, the first test fails (stale code), so it does test it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Upstream-Status: fork-only
Reason: A run reports whether the game makes memory executable and where the JIT was entered, and generated code is tested across threads
Issue: Sunshine-Off/NX2Linux#17

